# Literal matrix certificates for the marked point-core intersection

Seven native kernel words are intertwined with seven words in a conjugate
point core by the actual max4 actor `bridge * y^3 * bridge⁻¹`. Shared prefixes
reduce the calculation to 63 matrix products. `MarkedIntersection` uses these
identities to construct 128 distinct members; the extraspecial size bound
then proves exhaustiveness, without an 8192-by-8192 search.

All numerical identities are checked by kernel reduction. The witness data
come from the existing ATLAS max2 factor matrices and max4 actor, retaining
the original attribution in their source directories.
Source context: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Corollary 1.2.2(a) and Section 2.1,
printed pp.488--489. No normalizer placement follows from these identities.
-/

